#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:1
msgid "Dynamic Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:2
msgid "Overview and usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:4
msgid ""
"Dynamic Debugging lets developers step through unoptimized code from "
"optimized binaries. It largely removes the historical trade-off of runtime "
"performance for improved debuggability by providing both at the cost of "
"longer compile times and larger object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:6
msgid ""
"The feature is enabled from Clang with `-fdynamic-debugging` (disabled with "
"`-fno-dynamic-debugging`) and requires a compatible linker such as LLD. No "
"additional flags are required for linking dynamic debugging objects. Objects "
"compiled with dynamic debugging can be linked with objects compiled without "
"it. It also requires a compatible debugger (note that LLDB does not support "
"the feature)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:8
msgid ""
"The full unoptimized binary is compiled ahead of time along with the "
"optimized version, and all of its globals reference the optimized binary "
"(both data and code - so unoptimized functions call optimized ones). While "
"debugging, when a breakpoint is requested the debugger patches the optimized "
"function entry to jump to the unoptimized version. Because unoptimized "
"functions call optimized versions, continuing execution returns execution to "
"the optimized binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:10
msgid "Important info:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:11
msgid ""
"Compiler flags apply to both versions (except optimization level, which is "
"set to 0 for the unoptimized version)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:12
msgid ""
"Preprocessor definitions apply to both versions so the unoptimized version "
"may differ from a standalone \"debug\" build (consider debug and assert "
"macros such as NDEBUG)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:13
msgid ""
"Some optimizations are suppressed so the optimized object may be different "
"to an optimized object built without dynamic debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:14
msgid "There is a compile time and object file size impact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:15
msgid ""
"Linking an object file that has no strong external symbols multiple times "
"into the same ELF may result in a symbol redefinition linker error when "
"built with this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:17
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:19
msgid ""
"Currently the feature is only supported with the ELF file format. Non-x86 "
"targets are not supported yet; although they should work the feature has "
"only been tested on x86 platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:20
msgid "LLDB does not support Dynamic Debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:21
msgid "LLD does not support `--wrap=<symbol>` with Dynamic Debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:22
msgid "Dynamic Debugging with LTO is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:24
msgid ""
"When adding support for additional targets, `prepareForDynamicDebugging` "
"needs to be taught the correct `tail-pad-to-size` and `tail-pad-value` "
"attribute values, which would otherwise be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:26
msgid "Nested object design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:28
msgid ""
"The broad idea is that the unoptimized program (“inner object”) is compiled "
"and stored in a new section in the optimized version (“outer object\"). "
"“Nesting” the objects allows build systems and other tools to continue to "
"manage a single object file per translation unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:30
msgid "High level nested object design:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:32
msgid ""
"In the outer (optimized) module, globals with internal linkage not in a "
"COMDAT are “promoted” so they can be referenced by the inner (unoptimized) "
"module. We implement this by introducing aliases with external linkage with "
"suffixes unique to the translation unit. The suffix is “.dyndbg.<hash of "
"directory, file, and driver flags>”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:33
msgid ""
"The inner (unoptimized) module contains unoptimized copies of the outer "
"module’s functions. Their names are prefixed with “__dyndbg.”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:34
msgid ""
"Declarations corresponding to the originally external and now-promoted "
"globals in the outer module are added to the inner module. All global "
"references (function and data) in the inner module refer to the outer module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DynamicDebugging.md:35
msgid ""
"After linking, the inner ELF is still essentially an ET_REL object. It’s the "
"debugger’s job to extract, load, and apply relocations for the inner ELF."
msgstr ""

